  "$comment": "Differential on the bench, LDraw frame (-y up). The differential is LDraw's own assembly 65414c01 (casing 65414, drive gear 65413 clipped on, two 12T side gears and three 12T satellites 6589) turned so its axis runs along x at y=-100, z=0 (assembly origin (-3,-100,0)). Medium motor A at the origin, output up, carries a 12T bevel 6589 on a 2L axle at (0,-65,0): its axis meets the differential's at O'=(0,-100,0), 35 LDU (the 28T's pitch radius) from the pinion, and the 28T's centre (17,-100,0) is 17 LDU from O' (the 12T's pitch radius 15, plus the 2 LDU LDraw's own assembly seats its 12T bevels off the pitch cone, kinds/bevel.js SEAT_TOL_LDU), which keeps the 28T's teeth clear of the pinion's axle. The frame is the bevel bench's on both sides: Technic beams 7 standing upright on friction pins in the housing's side holes (x=40 on 2L pins, x=-60 on 3L pins: the casing reaches x=-35), and a Technic beam 3 across each pair's tops (x=60 and x=-80, y=-100) whose middle hole holds a side axle (left 4L x -95..-15, right 4L x 9..89). Frame and housing are one body.",
